infographic hierarchy-mindmap-level-gradient-compact-card
data
  title NoSQL is four families, not one
  desc Each wins on one known access shape and loses on the questions it wasn't built for
  root
    label NoSQL
    children
      - label Document
        desc MongoDB — denormalized self-contained docs, read whole in one lookup, no join
      - label Key-value
        desc Redis, DynamoDB — a hash map, fastest lookup by known id, no querying inside the value
      - label Wide-column
        desc Cassandra, Bigtable — partition-keyed rows, huge write throughput, no single primary
      - label Graph
        desc Neptune, Neo4j — nodes and edges first-class, cheap traversals (friends-of-friends)
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #8b5cf6
